$\begin{align}
\dfrac{z^7}{z^2}&=\dfrac{\overbrace{\cancel z\cdot \cancel z\cdot z\cdot z\cdot z\cdot z\cdot z}^\text{7 times}}{\underbrace{\cancel z\cdot \cancel z}_\text{2 times}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{z\cdot z\cdot z\cdot z\cdot z}_\text{5 times}
\\\\
\end{align}$

When powers have the same base $\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$. 

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{z^7}{z^2}&=z^{7-2}
\\\\
&=z^5
\end{align}$
